# "Whenever a Food is put into a graveyard from the battlefield": Bot2's Llanowar Elves is a Food because of Ygra, and
# Swords to Plowshares exiles it. It goes to exile, not to a graveyard, so Ygra's ability does not trigger (the stack is
# empty once the Swords has resolved) and Ygra gets no counters. Bot2 gains 1 life, the Elves' power.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Sol Ring
Ygra, Eater of All
Mox Pearl
Swords to Plowshares
Forest x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Forest x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Ygra, Eater of All.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Subtypes = Druid; Elf; Food
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Swords to Plowshares.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
? Stack.Count = 0
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Stack.Count = 0
Exile = Llanowar Elves
Bot2.Life = 21
Bot1.Battlefield.Ygra, Eater of All.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = (absent)
